    "heading": "MiCOM P841"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:73",
    "text": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:74",
    "text": "MiCOM P841: Multifunction Line Terminal Protection and Control IED",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:75",
    "text": "The MiCOM P841 is a multifunctional line terminal IED for control and back-up protection in transmission and sub-transmission feeder bays.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:76",
    "text": "The following Models are available:",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:77",
    "text": "MiCOM P841 Model A for Single Breaker Applications with 16 Inputs and 14 Outputs",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:78",
    "text": "MiCOM P841 Model B for Two Breaker Applications with 24 Inputs and 32 Outputs",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:79",
    "text": "Single or Three-phase auto-reclosing applications",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:80",
    "text": "The P841 Model A can be applied as a stand-alone solution for Auto-reclose and Check synch functionality for feeders controlled by a single circuit breaker.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:81",
    "text": "The P841 Model B can be applied as a stand-alone solution for Auto-reclose and Check synch functionality for Dual circuit breakers applications such as ring bus/mesh corner formations and the breaker-and-a-half configurations.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:82",
    "text": "Contractual warranty",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:83",
    "text": "Period : 2 years",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:84",
    "text": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:85",
    "text": "The logic capabilities of the MiCOM P841 products are extremely versatile, for instance managing leader-follower reclosing schemes in case of dual breaker applications.",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:86",
    "text": "Transmission-class circuit breaker failure protection for one or two breakers. The breaker failure protection may be initiated from internal protection within the P841, and also from external devices.",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:87",
    "text": "Single pole and three-pole breaker operation is supported, with independent supervision & condition monitoring statistics for each pole",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:88",
    "text": "Trip circuit supervision, control, and interlocking schemes can be designed in graphical support software.",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:89",
    "text": "Ancillary applications include use of the P841 for binary I/O concentration, disturbance recording, or as a gateway to SCADA protocols and IEC 61850",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:90",
    "text": "Multiple protection elements are provided, such as directional overcurrent, earth fault, voltage and frequency. This allows P841 to be deployed as a back-up IED in transmission applications, or as the Main 2 protection solution for sub-transmission systems.",
    "heading": "Benefits"
  },
